<h2>Context</h2>
<p>
  The initial integration snapshot mixed two incompatible framework targets:
</p>
<ul>
  <li>The legacy prototype <code>CliApp/FluxEncoderCli.csproj</code> targeted <code>net8.0</code> with a hardcoded <code>win-x64</code> runtime identifier and did not compile (<code>CODE_AUDIT.md</code> A-02).</li>
  <li>The concept sources and design references in <code>FluxEncoderEngine/</code> targeted .NET 10 with NativeAOT publishing.</li>
</ul>
<p>
  Both the local development host and the pinned GitLab CI build image (<code>{{ generated.project.ciImage }}</code>) provide the .NET 10 SDK. Nothing in the architecture requires .NET 8 binary compatibility:
</p>
<ul>
  <li><code>psm/FluxEncoder.psm1</code> invokes the published CLI executable as an out-of-process child command rather than loading FluxEncoder assemblies into the PowerShell AppDomain, so the PowerShell runtime version does not constrain FluxEncoder's target framework.</li>
  <li>No external library consumers, binary plugins, or published NuGet libraries exist.</li>
  <li>No target deployment environment restricted to a .NET 8-only runtime has been identified.</li>
</ul>

<h2>Decision</h2>

{{ specTable({
  caption: "ADR 0001 POLICY CLAUSES",
  headers: ["Clause", "Specification"],
  codeCols: [0],
  rows: [
    ["1. Single Target", "All production and test projects target <code>net10.0</code> (LTS, supported until November 2028). The value is declared once in <code>Directory.Build.props</code>."],
    ["2. No Multi-Targeting", "<code>net8.0</code> is not multi-targeted. It will be added only if a concrete compatibility requirement is recorded in a new ADR that supersedes ADR 0001."],
    ["3. SDK Pinning", "<code>global.json</code> pins the 10.0 SDK feature band with <code>rollForward: latestFeature</code>, allowing any 10.0.x SDK at or above <code>10.0.100</code> while preventing silent upgrades to a future major SDK."],
    ["4. Publish-Time RIDs", "Normal builds do not hardcode a <code>RuntimeIdentifier</code>. Runtime identifiers and NativeAOT are publish-time choices configured per release artifact under <code>TSKE015.1</code>."],
    ["5. Legacy Archive", "The legacy <code>CliApp</code> project is removed from the solution build and archived in <code>archive/legacy-cli/</code>."]
  ]
}) }}

<h2>Consequences</h2>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Unified static analysis:</strong> Maintaining a single target framework yields one deterministic set of nullable reference, trimming, and AOT analyzer diagnostics without <code>#if NET8_0</code> conditional compilation branches.</li>
  <li><strong>NativeAOT readiness:</strong> Choosing NativeAOT at publish time remains open across Windows, Linux, and macOS for both <code>x64</code> and <code>arm64</code> targets.</li>
  <li><strong>Lifecycle review:</strong> This decision will be re-evaluated before .NET 10 reaches end of support in November 2028 to transition cleanly to the next LTS release.</li>
</ul>
